 **Collaboration** | ✅ *CodeWriter* produced clean, well-commented code; *CodeReviewer* and *CodeDebugger* ensured a smooth, error-free run |\n\n### Areas for Potential Improvement\n- The output CRS remains undefined — if a known CRS (e.g., a projected coordinate system) can be identified, assigning it explicitly would improve interoperability.\n- The garbled field name `Ãû³Æ` persists in the output (as it was preserved from input). If the true field name is known to be `名称`, a renaming step could be added for clarity.\n\n---\n\n## 4. 🤝 Agent Contributions\n\n| Agent | Role | Contribution |\n|---|---|---|\n| **DataReader** | Data Inspection | Provided comprehensive metadata summaries of both input shapefiles, identifying encoding issues and spatial extents |\n| **CodeWriter** | Code Generation | Authored the `clip_roads.py` script with proper GIS logic, encoding handling, and defensive safeguards |\n| **CodeReviewer** | Code Review | Validated the script's logic, identified potential edge cases |\n| **CodeDebugger** | Execution & Debugging | Ensured the script ran successfully and produced correct output |\n| **CodeFinisher** | Final Summary | Compiled this comprehensive report with metadata registration |\n\n---\n\n**✅ Subtask 1 is complete.** The clipped road shapefile is ready at `coder/subtask_1/road_clipped.shp` containing 2 features with all original attributes intact.", additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, name='coder', id='297f97c2-c7a6-4b03-af13-15737b61a121'), AIMessage(content='CONTINUE: The required output file `road_clipped.shp` was found at `coder/subtask_1/road_clipped.shp`. The clipped Shapefile has been successfully generated with all original attribute fields preserved, containing 2 LineString features clipped to the `area.shp` boundary.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, name='codeReviewer', id='f2c177fb-aa1a-45a0-a92b-af2b61da6ff6'), AIMessage(content='Coder', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, name='manager')], 'user_q